  "defect_found_and_fixed": {
    "symptom": "decision_loop after a qualifying candidate already existed",
    "root_cause": "choose_strategy is one-shot per assessment, and the prompt said so, but the tool did not enforce it. Re-issuing it for a strategy whose status was already 'selected' changed nothing and was caught only later by the generic repeated-action guard, which stopped the task without calling finish.",
    "fixes": [
      "agents/harness/tools.py::_choose_strategy rejects a repeat decision for a hypothesis that already has a selected strategy and names the legal next actions.",
      "agents/harness/tools.py::available_actions adds a 'qualifying_candidate_found' stage exposing finish as the next action once a supported child exists."
    ],
    "regression_tests": [
      "tests/test_harness.py::test_repeated_strategy_decision_is_rejected_with_legal_next_actions",
      "tests/test_harness.py::test_qualifying_candidate_exposes_finish_not_strategy_decision"
    ]
  },
  "budget_and_size_caveat": "The parent-derived catalogue is larger than the original phenol catalogue: 70 actions and 40 unique valid products versus 24 actions and 16 products. Budgets were left unchanged (max_evaluations=11, max_edits=3, max_steps=45). The phenol arm therefore operates on a different feasible-space size than the earlier v10 run and cannot be compared to it on magnitude. Cross-parent comparison here is about mechanism and failure mode, not effect size.",
  "honest_limitations": [
    "One real run per parent per arm; no repetition, so no variance estimate.",
    "The rule arm never found a qualifying product on any parent (0/3), so it is a weak baseline.",
    "The agent found qualifying products on 1 of 3 parents in the fixed study; this is a single observation.",
    "Reachability scores are computed separately and hidden from both policies.",
    "No docking, no biological validation, and the 0.01 threshold is unchanged.",
    "The pre-fix aniline result is a defect artifact and is not evidence about agent capability."
  ]
}